course: dictionary
lesson: 4275
title: Greatest and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Greatest is the top form of the adjective great, just as biggest is the top form of big. Use it when one thing is more than all the others: the greatest number, the greatest adventure.
explain: Greatest can also mean best or most important, as in the greatest player of all time. «Helping those in greatest need» means helping the people who need help most, so here greatest means most.
explain: In maths, greatest asks for the largest number or amount. «Greatest common factor» is the largest number that divides exactly into two numbers. Check your meaning by swapping in "most" or "largest" and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Great, greater, greatest: one thing, then two things compared, then all of them.
fact: «Greatest» means the biggest or most of all.
fact: «Greatest» also means the best or most important.
fact: The greatest 3-digit number is 999.
fact: Greatest common factor and greatest common divisor are two names for the same idea.
exercise: «Fair ways to share something scarce include drawing lots, a waiting list and helping those in greatest need.» In this sentence, what does greatest mean? | Youngest | Smallest | *Most | Fairest
exercise: What is the greatest 3-digit number? | 100 | 990 | 1000 | *999
exercise: What is the greatest common factor of 12 and 18? | *6 | 2 | 3 | 36
test: «Choosing your friends is favouritism.» In «the greatest inventors», what does greatest mean? | The loudest | The smallest | *The most important or best | The youngest
test: Which is the greatest of these numbers: 407, 470, 704, 740? | 704 | *740 | 407 | 470
exam: «Fair ways to share something scarce include drawing lots, a waiting list and helping those in greatest need.» Which word means the same as greatest here? | Least | Shortest | *Most | Quietest
